On the first DDG-1000, this agreement means that the yard will receive approximately $3 billion in work. This agreement is a testament to the highly skilled and hardworking men and women of Bath Iron Works. It's also a win for the Navy. It will give the Navy cutting edge destroyers at affordable prices.

Over the past several years, I have worked so hard to ensure that the Navy has the funds that it needs to meet our military requirements. More recently, I've also worked hard with the Navy and Bath Iron Works to bring the two sides together to urge them to conclude these vital negotiations. This agreement will help to ensure a steady workload for our shipyard for years to come.
